@page "/privacy"
@{ ViewData["Title"]="Privacy"; }
<h1>Privacy</h1>
<p>Browsing and installing need no account. Publisher sign-in uses GitHub's public profile identifier and login. The portal does not request repository or email permissions and does not retain the GitHub access token.</p>
<p>Registration stores your GitHub identifier, login, chosen publisher name, public signing key, channel names, publishing permissions and registration date. Published package metadata and signatures are public. Unlisted channels remain accessible to anyone who knows their address.</p>
<p>Account cookies keep you signed in; a separate optional viewer cookie reveals unlisted channels in your browser. Theme preferences stay in browser storage. The server also keeps staged publication data and operational failure logs. Hosting infrastructure may keep its own request logs.</p>
<p>Contact the portal operator for account and retention questions. Removing a registration does not remove already published signed history.</p>
